;;; An hrule whose conclusion is an `and` inside an `and` proposes one
;;; fact headed `and`, a commitment no state can hold.
;;;
;;; A nested `(and …)` in an hrule: the inner one was a template headed `and`,
;;; and as the first conjunct it was the one the hypothesis layer read
;;; (`hrule-and.ein`), so H was `{(and (p a) (q a))}`, one candidate over the
;;; relation `and`, and R two states, the second holding `(and (p a) (q a))`;
;;; `(r a)` was proposed by nothing. A conclusion is read flat at any depth, so
;;; it is three conjuncts, and the right answer is `hrule-and.ein`'s: refused at
;;; load, an hrule's conclusion being one fact (Q-M1f.271).
;;;
(relation p Thing :why "p {?3}")
(relation q Thing :why "q {?3}")
(relation r Thing :why "r {?3}")
(hrule h () :match () :assert (and (and (p a) (q a)) (r a)) :why "propose p and q, and r, of a")
